{"id": 4744, "doi": "10.4038/slja.v21i2.4744", "title": "Epinephrine toxicity : An avoidable fatal complication due to iatrogenic overdose", "abstract": "<p>Epinephrine is used as an additive to local anaesthetic solutions. Large doses of epinephrine used in local anaesthesia can cause toxic manifestations as in our case in a young patient posted for Tympanoplasty.</p> <p>DOI: <a href=\"http://dx.doi.org/10.4038/slja.v21i2.4744\">http://dx.doi.org/10.4038/slja.v21i2.4744</a></p>", "keywords": ["epinephrine", "epinephrine toxicity", "local anaesthesia"], "authors": [{"first_name": "Charu", "last_name": "Neema", "institution": "", "country": "IN", "email": "charu.neema@gmail.com", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "Sahil", "last_name": "Kapur", "institution": "", "country": "IN", "email": "", "orcid": ""}], "section": "Case Reports", "pages": "72-73", "date_published": "2013-06-25T00:00:00+00:00", "date_submitted": "2012-10-14T11:57:54+00:00", "license_name": "", "license_link": "", "files": [{"label": "PDF", "language": "en", "url": "https://slja.sljol.info/articles/4744/files/4744-1-20340-1-10-20130625.pdf"}], "references": "", "volume": 21, "number": "2", "year": 2013, "issue_id": 534}